re are even no OTB games starting from this position. } 16. f4 { Protecting e5 but now we can at least transpose to the 16.a3 line by playing 16...a5. } Qf8 $2 { The queen is very well placed here covering dark squares and it was our original idea before publishing the course. Unfortunately it just doesn't work. } 17. a3 { The only try. } Bxa3 18. Ne4 Bb4 { Forcing a weakening move. } 19. c3 Be7 20. b4 { Otherwise the pawn on b3 was hanging. } Ra8 21. Bc5 $1 { This is much better for White according to Stockfish 12 while Stockfish 11 considers this position as equal. Unfortunately for Black it is the new version of the engine which is right. } Bxc5+ 22. bxc5 Rxf4 { What else? Black is completely paralyzed. } 23. Nf6+ Rxf6 24. exf6 Qxf6 { Black is doing well materially but the bishop on c8 remains terrible. With the best play Black shouldn't survive. } 25. c4 $18 { with Qa5 is one way to proceed. } 
